<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!-- Blazor. References the Api project for its contract types [CLAUDE.md
       section 4]. It reaches data only by calling the Api over HTTP.

       That reference is the whole Api, not a contracts assembly, so Data and
       Npgsql are in this project's compiled closure even though nothing here
       uses them. Pipeline is not, so no stage is reachable from here. A
       contracts assembly is the fix and it is carried from phase 0 to phase 9
       in BUILD_PLAN rather than built for a UI that does not exist yet [O.3].

       Blazor Server rather than WebAssembly. A WebAssembly Ui cannot carry a
       project reference to the Api at all: the Api carries a FrameworkReference
       to Microsoft.AspNetCore.App, which has no browser-wasm runtime pack, and
       the build fails with NETSDK1082. Reported in the 0.1 commit body. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\StockResearcherLab.Api\StockResearcherLab.Api.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
